A||||9||Formula88||I LOVE the Fiero Store!||||10||
Z||000000||Formula88||03-02-2001||09:51 AM||||A company with great customer service!!!<P>I ordered a input shaft bearing for my Getrag last Saturday, and had it shipped 2nd day air, cuz well, my baby isn't driveable without it.  To make a long story short, as of today, the part still hadn't arrived.  I called the Fiero Store and not only did they track the shipment down (UPS screwed up, not them), they made sure it was going to be delivered today, and they got the shipping charges credited back from UPS and are going to credit me for the shipping.  Some may say that this is the minimum expected of a company, but I've found lately that's not the case more often than not.  It's such a pleasure to do business with a company that has quick, courteous, and efficient customer service.  They've got my businees, oh YEA!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||terryk||03-02-2001||11:48 AM||||Yep, they're expensive but they are fast and great support. Usually worth the extra money.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||03-02-2001||11:51 AM||||I've also been very happy with the Fiero Store!  I've gotten a lot of little things to fix up my 88 GT over the last month or so.  They've always had what I needed in stock and shipped things out promptly.  It sure makes getting stuff for our cars a lot easier  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||10
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||03-02-2001||02:50 PM||||Ive dumped alot of money at The Fiero Store in the last months... Im <B><I>VERY</I></B> happy with them. All the things came very fast...<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-02-2001||03:31 PM||||I had good dealings with them also... <P>but nothing but problems with UPS.. after fighting to get springs for a friend i sent them out UPS ground and for over 2 weeks they had no record of my shipping them even though i had a tracking # and the UPS man that comes to the office "remember he'd picked up a heavy box" thats really what it says on the loss report.. i got the run around till monday and i'll be getting a check to reimburse me for the springs in 7-10 business days and the shipping charges won't be billed to the office! what ever happen to the box.. i've got NO FRIGGEN clue! I'll be sure to let everone know if they really do pony up a check. that was $150 out of Visa's pocket!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and over 3 months of waiting and calling and pleading. CORK sucking Iceholes! but i'm not bitter...<P>humm.. wonder if he wants a set of Panoz hand made race springs...  hummmm... <BR> ||||reg||1
