Z||000008||AusFiero||03-03-2001||04:10 AM||||I can relate to tthe courier stuff. I do a lot of work for a Pontiac spare part simporter in Australia. Over the last 6 months 2 bonnets that got here with no trouble from America have been damaged by idiot courier company employees seeing this big flat plywood box (yes we even have to box them to try get them there safely)as a great pallet and use them to stack freight on...them pick up with the forklift..<P>I am sure last time I read stand upright only it meant just that. Maybe I will have to ask my wife to get upright for me.<P>Oh and they also had treat like eggs stickers etc...Courier employees obviously like scrambled eggs.<P>A 3rd bonnet we do not know the fate of...probably too good a pallet for the forklift driver to release it.||||reg||1
